NAME
     nm - the symbols in an object file

SYNOPSIS
     nm [-a] [-D] [-g] [-n] [-p] [-r] [-u] [-S] FILE...

DESCRIPTION
     nm prints the symbol table: the value, the kind (T for text, D for
     data, B for bss, U for undefined, and so on) and the name.

OPTIONS
     -a   all symbols, including the debugging ones
     -D   the dynamic symbols
     -g   only the global ones
     -n   sort by value
     -p   do not sort
     -r   reverse the order
     -u   only the undefined ones
     -S   print sizes as well

SEE ALSO
     readelf(1), ldd(1), strings(1)
